+    Rule:
+    - Treat each scattered panel as one sprite cropped to its bounding box.
+    - In each panel, the dominant non-black color is that panel's main color; any lone
+      other non-black pixel is a pointer naming the panel directly above it.
+    - The panel that is never pointed to is the bottom layer, and the panel with no pointer
+      pixel is the top layer. Overlay panels in that chain order, painting only main-color
+      cells and treating black holes and pointer pixels as transparent.
+
